# @@TITLE_EN@@ · @@TITLE_AR@@

An independent web application generated by the GAIE Master Build Engine (layer L16)
from a `gaie.spec/1` requirement specification. It needs only Python 3.11+ (standard
library) to run; the browser test additionally needs Node.js 20+ and Playwright.
It has **no runtime dependency on the engineering hub**: the hub is referenced only in
`.gaie/link.json`, which records the hub revision and templates used to generate it.

تطبيق ويب مستقل أنشأه محرك البناء الرئيسي. يعمل بمكتبة Python القياسية فقط، وواجهته
ثنائية اللغة (العربية من اليمين إلى اليسار، والإنجليزية من اليسار إلى اليمين)، ولا يعتمد
أثناء التشغيل على مركز الهندسة.

## Run

```sh
python3 manage.py migrate          # create data/app.sqlite3 (gitignored)
python3 manage.py seed             # optional: load SYNTHETIC sample records
python3 manage.py serve            # http://127.0.0.1:8000
```

Options: `serve --port 0` picks a free port, `--db PATH` uses another database file.
The server binds to loopback only; see [Security](#security) before exposing it.

## Test

```sh
python3 -I manage.py test --report /tmp/report.json   # unit + API integration tests
node tests/e2e/ui.e2e.mjs                             # browser E2E (Playwright + Chromium)
```

- Unit tests (`tests/test_validation.py`, `tests/test_migrations.py`) cover validation of
  types, required fields, maximum lengths, enumerations, defaults and the migrations.
- API integration tests (`tests/test_api.py`) start the real HTTP server on a free port and
  cover CRUD for every entity, status codes 201/400/404/405/409/413/415, relation checks,
  security headers, cross-origin refusal and SQL-injection inertness.
- The E2E test creates, edits and deletes records through the UI in every locale, checks
  labels, keyboard reachability, CSP and that no request leaves the application origin.
  Set `APP_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE` to use a specific Chromium binary. `package.json` pins the
  reviewed Playwright version for `npm ci --ignore-scripts`.

