## Security

- Input validation for every field (type, required, maximum length/value, enumeration,
  strict dates and e-mail), unknown and read-only fields refused, body size limit
  (@@MAX_BODY@@ bytes), JSON only, duplicate JSON keys refused.
- Parameterized SQL; identifiers come only from the validated schema.
- Headers on every response: `Content-Security-Policy` (`default-src 'self'`,
  `frame-ancestors 'none'`, no inline code), `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`,
  `X-Frame-Options: DENY`, `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, COOP/CORP.
- CSRF-safe design: writes need `Content-Type: application/json` and a same-origin
  request (`Origin`/`Sec-Fetch-Site` checked); no CORS headers are ever sent.
- No secrets in the repository, no shell, no `eval`; the frontend never uses `innerHTML`.
- **No user authentication yet.** The server refuses non-loopback binding unless
  `--allow-network` is given; put it behind an authenticating proxy first (open item).

